  "query_preview": "(This evening through Thursday)...\nIssued at 210 PM EDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon...\n\nA surface trough was near I-70 early this afternoon. Radar shows \nisolated showers developing, from just east of central Indiana into \nOhio. Scattered to broken cumulus covered central Indiana.\n\nWith the boundary in the area and some instability, isolated showers \nremain possible. Will continue to monitor in case coverage becomes \nenough to mention them in the forecast.\n\nTonight,,,\n\nThe isolated showers may linger until early evening, but again \ncoverage will likely be too low to mention. Otherwise, the cumulus \nwill gradually dissipate, leaving mostly clear to clear skies. The \npartial lunar eclipse should be visible (greatest eclipse is at 1213 \nAM EDT).\n\nLight winds along with the mostly clear skies will set the stage for \nsome patchy fog again tonight. With some drying occurring today, \nthere won't be as much dense fog around though. These conditions \nwill allow temperatures to get below blended guidance, so lowered \nmin temperatures a bit.\n\nFriday and Saturday...\n\nHigh pressure will provide dry conditions. Highs will be in the \nlower to middle 80s with lows in the upper 50s Friday night.\n\nSaturday night through Tuesday...\n\nAn upper level high will push its way into the area during this \nperiod, bringing a return of hot and humid conditions. \n\nBefore the warmer air arrives, convection will try and ride around \nthe upper high Saturday night. For now believe these will dissipate \nbefore reaching central Indiana, but some debris clouds from these \nmay linger into Sunday.\n\nHighs will warm from the upper 80s/lower 90s Sunday to the lower and \nmiddle 90s by Tuesday. Southwest winds will bring dewpoints \npotentially back to near 70 by Tuesday. Heat indices near 100 may \noccur most areas by Tuesday.\n\nWednesday and beyond...\n\nThe upper high will still be the predominant influence mid-week next \nweek, but it may shift just far enough away to allow for rain \nchances to return. Will have some low PoPs but with low confidence.\n\nHeat will continue, with highs mainly in the 90s again on Wednesday. \nIf the upper high moves far enough away, temperatures may cool into \nthe upper 80s to lower 90s on Thursday. \n\nThe persistent heat may lead to the need for a Heat Advisory, even \nif heat indices don't meet criteria.",
